<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  rocket-saturn-v: the Saturn V of Apollo 11. Generated by design/build_model.py.
  Z-up, metres. The view keeps the vehicle at the origin and moves the world (block RocketView). Every
  part that separates is its own link: "sic" (first stage), "interstage" (S-II aft interstage ring),
  "let" (launch escape tower), "sii" (second stage with the S-II/S-IVB interstage); "upper" is the
  S-IVB, instrument unit, adapter and Apollo spacecraft. Until its separation a part rides at its place
  in the stack (the link poses equal the vehicle attitude, the visuals sit along the link x axis from
  the S-IC base); after it the block SpentStage flies it ballistically. Approximate shapes, true
  lengths and diameters within a few metres. The plumes stretch with the thrust of their stage.
-->
